<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Kourion</h1><p class="st-meta">1100 BCE – 312 BCE (approx.) · capital Kourion</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Cypriot kingdom on a clifftop above the south coast, remembered for the sanctuary of Apollo Hylates and for its king's betrayal at the Battle of Salamis in 497 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kourion arose in the Episkopi area of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, near a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a> settlement, in the 11th century BCE. Its Greek inhabitants claimed descent from settlers from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/argos">Argos</a>. By the 7th century BCE it was one of the island's city-kingdoms, listed among the Cypriot rulers who paid tribute to the Assyrian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esarhaddon">Esarhaddon</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kings ruled a fertile territory along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kouris-river">Kouris</a> river. The sanctuary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanctuary-of-apollo-hylates">Apollo Hylates</a>, god of the woodland, was its chief cult centre, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luigi-palma-di-cesnola">Luigi Palma di Cesnola</a> claimed to have found a rich gold and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> hoard there, the so-called Curium treasure, though its true findspots are doubtful. Kourion followed the Cypriot syllabary and Greek institutions, under Assyrian and then Achaemenid overlordship.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionian-revolt">Ionian Revolt</a>, King Stasanor deserted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-salamis-in-cyprus">Battle of Salamis</a> in 497 BCE. Later King Pasicrates aided Alexander at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tyre">Tyre</a>. The monarchy was abolished under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-i-soter">Ptolemy I</a> c. 312 BCE, and Kourion flourished as a Roman and early Christian city until earthquakes in the 4th century CE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1100 BCE – 312 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Greece and the Aegean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:37.81%;width:15.68%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1100 BCE – 312 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century-bce">12th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kourion</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Stasanor, Pasicrates</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek religion; cult of Apollo Hylates</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arcado-Cypriot Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/cyprus">Cyprus</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kourion, Curium</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-706&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kourion" aria-label="Kingdom of Kourion on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5515 923 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Kourion lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5835 1179L6140 1251M5835 1179L5772 1297"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6140 1251h0M5772 1297h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5835 1179h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5835 1179h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kourion. <a href="/atlas?year=-706&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kourion">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

